[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/pulls/993","id":4283787805,"node_id":"PR_kwDOSeuyxc7_VWod","html_url":"https://github.com/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/pull/993","diff_url":"https://github.com/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/pull/993.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/pull/993.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/issues/993","number":993,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"feat(pipeline): delete the max generation depth and the depth concept","user":{"login":"saeedkolivand","id":51081940,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMDgxOTQw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51081940?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand","html_url":"https://github.com/saeedkolivand","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Deletes the `max` generation depth and the depth concept entirely. **86 files, +788 / −9051.** Fourth of five PRs in the multi-stage pipeline programme, after #990, #991 and #992.\n\n## Why\n\n`max` cost roughly 12+ model calls per run — a section-by-section fan-out plus an `llm_judge` stage whose output was Warning-only model opinion that nothing in the app acted on. That is pure token spend. #992 already cut the apply flow over to the staged quality pipeline unconditionally, so the depth selectors were steering a choice that no longer existed.\n\nThe staged pipeline is now the only one: `analyze_job → match_evidence → strategy → draft → cover_letter → validate → repair → humanize`.\n\n## Deleted\n\n**Rust** — `stages/judge.rs`, `stages/section_gen.rs`, `section_prompts.rs`, `max_pipeline()`/`MAX_STAGES`, `regenerate_max_entry`, the section-observer half of the run hooks, `Budget::RESUME_MAX`, `MAX_RUN_FIXED_SECS`, `GenerationDepth` and the request's `depth` field. `types_max.rs` trims to `ProjectOut` and `assemble.rs` to `render_project` — both load-bearing for #990's deterministic projects normalization.\n\n**Renderer** — `DepthSelector`, `SectionTimeline`, `GenerationDepthPreferences`, the `useGenerationDepth` slice, `lib/generate/generation-depth.ts`, and the pipeline machine's per-section fold.\n\n`TailoredResumePanel` survives this PR deliberately — see below.\n\n## Existing user data keeps working\n\nThis is where a deletion this size actually fails, so it got the most attention. Three things are deliberately kept as read-only historic vocabulary, because users have runs recorded at all three depths:\n\n- `RunRow.depth` stays a plain column, now always writing `\"quality\"`. **No migration** — verified correct by executing SQL probes that insert pre-deletion rows on retired stages and exercising the read, snapshot, write and import paths.\n- `GENERATION_DEPTHS` in `packages/shared`, so an old `max` row renders \"Max\" rather than a raw token.\n- `pipeline.stage.sections|assemble|llm_judge` translations.\n\nThat last one was a **caught regression, not a plan**. The first pass froze the depth vocabulary with a test, then deleted the stage names — which live on the *same rows*, of the *same feature*, rendered by the *same component* one line away. Review caught it by rendering a stored run and seeing three untranslated wire tokens next to a translated one. The fix-round enumeration then found two further render sites, because the live stage label replays from the last persisted event on reconnect.\n\n## Behavior change worth stating\n\nOn a **historic `max` run**, regenerating one role (`SectionKey::Experience(n)`) no longer has its per-entry path, so it falls through to `regenerate_one_section` and rewrites the **whole Work Experience section**. The deleted path had guaranteed the opposite. This is inherent to deleting `max` and was already the documented degrade — no code change — but it is user-visible and belongs in the release notes.\n\n## Review\n\n`rust-backend-architect` APPROVE, `frontend-reviewer` BLOCK→resolved. Both ran every gate themselves and mutation-tested each claimed guard rather than reading them. Three findings are worth recording:\n\n**Two functions went dead with zero signal.** An author verified a helper's last consumer and stopped one hop short — that consumer was itself deleted by this PR. Both are `pub` in a `pub` module of a lib crate, so `dead_code` structurally cannot fire; they survived 4175 tests, `clippy --all-targets --all-features -D warnings`, and the architecture suite. Found by deleting them and compiling. Applying the same method one hop further found a **third** (`sections::entry_range`, whose only callers lived in a test file this PR deletes) plus a chain of private helpers.\n\n**A \"guard\" that only tested itself.** `PIPELINE_RUN_DEPTHS_HISTORIC` had zero production consumers — the component interpolates the label key directly. Truncating the constant reddened only the test's own assertion about the constant. Dropped; the label assertions that do hold were kept.\n\n**The showcase separator lost its only pin.** Changing `PROJECT_SEPARATOR` from `\" · \"` to `\" - \"` passed the whole suite, because the deleted `max_test.rs` had held the only verbatim render assertions. That glyph feeds `consistency::tier_of` / `project_entry_starts` on the Projects section, so it is now pinned and mutation-tested.\n\n## Scope note\n\n`TailoredResumePanel` moves to PR-5. The first pass deleted it, then found it also hosts the agentic \"Improve this résumé\" flow, which nothing in the apply flow ports — so it reverted rather than orphaning a feature shipped six commits earlier. PR-5 already owns `improve_resume`, so the panel dies there alongside it. Here it keeps only the quality run: its depth picker and section timeline are gone, so nothing dead is left behind for a PR.\n\nAlso swept: the orphaned `pipeline.section.*` subtree (~17 keys × 2 locales), each verified unreferenced first — given the HIGH above is exactly what happens when a key looks dead and is not.\n\n## Testing\n\n`cargo test --workspace` 4175 passed / 26 ignored + 18 architecture + 3 eval · `cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features --locked -D warnings` clean · `cargo fmt --check` · `gen:ipc:check` + `gen:prompts:check` · `pnpm typecheck` 13/13 · `pnpm test` 485 files / 7118 tests · `pnpm lint:strict --max-warnings 0` · en/de parity, zero orphans.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Résumé generation now uses a single staged quality workflow.\n  * Removed generation-depth selection from résumé creation and settings.\n  * Section progress tracking and section-by-section regeneration are no longer available.\n  * Historical runs retain readable labels for retired stages and depth values.\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Improved recovery when a run fails before live status updates are available.\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Updated guidance and translations for the current résumé generation process.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-08-14T23:17:20Z","updated_at":"2026-08-15T02:19:57Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"e13d30a22cc463208d577936f5a3d5ede2095221","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[{"id":10964600421,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSeuyxc8AAAACjYqGZQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/labels/documentation","name":"documentation","color":"0075ca","default":true,"description":"Documentation and markdown"},{"id":11212541200,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSeuyxc8AAAACnFHNEA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/labels/app/desktop","name":"app/desktop","color":"0e8a16","default":false,"description":"Changes to apps/desktop"},{"id":11212541282,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSeuyxc8AAAACnFHNYg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/labels/pkg/shared","name":"pkg/shared","color":"1abc9c","default":false,"description":"Changes to packages/shared"},{"id":11212541489,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSeuyxc8AAAACnFHOMQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/labels/pkg/translations","name":"pkg/translations","color":"20c997","default":false,"description":"Changes to packages/translations"},{"id":11212541572,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSeuyxc8AAAACnFHOhA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/labels/rust","name":"rust","color":"dea584","default":false,"description":"Rust backend (apps/desktop/src-tauri)"},{"id":11212541661,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSeuyxc8AAAACnFHO3Q","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/labels/frontend","name":"frontend","color":"7057ff","default":false,"description":"React renderer (apps/desktop/src/renderer)"}],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/pulls/993/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/pulls/993/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/issues/993/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/r